            <ArticleTitle>Jejunal diverticulitis with localized perforation and intramesenteric abscess.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1173-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare case of a 69-yr-old white man with jejunal diverticulitis with localized perforation and intramesenteric abscess formation. This entity is often overlooked as a cause of acute abdominal pain in the elderly. Although the clinical diagnosis is difficult, a high index of suspicion should warrant a computed tomography scan or enteroclysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
